On Sep 22, 9:14=A0am, pa...@alt.org (Pasi Kallinen) wrote:
> This patch adds a new configuration option MSGTYPE.
>
> This allows the user to configure whether a message always waits for --mo=
re--,
> or if it's never shown, or if it's never shown more than once in row.
>
> Patch DB:http://bilious.homelinux.org/?397
> Direct URL:http://bilious.homelinux.org/~paxed/nethack/nh343-msgtype.diff
>
> The format is
> MSGTYPE=3Dfoo "string to match"
> Where "foo" is one of "hide", "stop" or "norep", and the string to match
> is a message to be matched, with '*' and '?' wildcard expansion.
>
> "hide" hides the message, so it's never shown.
> "stop" always prompts for --more-- after the message.
> "norep" shows the message, but not again if no other message is shown in =
between.
>
> ("noshow" is an alias to "hide", and "more" is an alias to "stop")
>
> For example:
>
> # displacing pets
> MSGTYPE=3Dhide =A0"You displaced *"
> # items on floor
> MSGTYPE=3Dnorep "You see here a *"
> MSGTYPE=3Dnorep "You see here an *"
> # delayed instadeaths
> MSGTYPE=3Dstop =A0"You are slowing down."
> MSGTYPE=3Dstop =A0"You find it hard to breathe."
> MSGTYPE=3Dstop =A0"You are turning a little *"
>
> --
